cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or evaluation protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "InventOR: Can Large Language Models Set Reorder Points and Safety Stocks? Industrial Evidence Against ERP and Data-Driven Benchmarks"
authors:
  - family-names: Dressino
    given-names: Aris
    affiliation: "TUM School of Management, Technical University of Munich"
version: 1.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DressPD/inventor_public"
abstract: >-
  A confidentiality-screened public release of InventOR: analysis code, the
  approved masked panel, three frozen original generations rescaled to that
  panel and three fresh masked generations, sanitized provenance with retained
  amendment histories, APA seventh-edition manuscript sources, and an integrity
  manifest. Credential-free replay reproduces six-run evidence, the matched
  338-pair table and figure sources on one underlying panel, not six independent
  datasets. Prepared version 1.3.0 has no new archive DOI assigned here.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - inventory management
  - operations research
  - reproducibility
  - prompt engineering
  - material-level inventory control
